\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. From north and south and east and west,
\par When shall the peoples, long unblest,
\par All find their everlasting rest,
\par O Christ, in Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When shall the climes of ageless snow
\par Be with the Gospel light aglow,
\par And all men their Redeemer know,
\par O Christ, in Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When on each southern balmy coast,
\par Shall ransomed men, in countless host,
\par Rise, heart and voice, to make sweet boast,
\par O Christ, in Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O when in all orient lands,
\par From cities white and flaming sands,
\par Shall men lift dedicated hands,
\par O Christ, to Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O when shall heathen darkness roll
\par Away in light, from pole to pole,
\par And endless day by every soul
\par Be founded in Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Bring, Lord, the long-predicted hour,
\par The ages' diadem and flower,
\par When all shall find their refuge-tower
\par And home in Thee.     
\par                     Amen.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

